  },
  "blocks": [
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Lists are among the most common structures in long-form technical and reference writing, and they rarely stay flat. A single outline can mix bulleted groups with numbered sequences, nest one inside the other, and carry links partway through an item. This fixture exercises those shapes: a bulleted list whose second item contains a nested bulleted list, whose first item in turn contains a nested numbered list, three levels deep in total.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [{ "text": "Outline", "marks": [] }]
    },
    {
      "kind": "bulleted-list",
      "items": [
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                { "text": "Flat items with a link mid-item: the ", "marks": [] },
                { "text": "HTML specification", "marks": [{ "type": "link", "href": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/grouping-content.html#the-ul-element" }] },
                { "text": " permits both ordered and unordered nesting to arbitrary depth.", "marks": [] }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                { "text": "A second item that opens a nested bulleted list:", "marks": [] }
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "bulleted-list",
              "items": [
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "kind": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        { "text": "The first nested item, which itself opens a numbered sequence:", "marks": [] }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "numbered-list",
                      "start": 1,
                      "items": [
                        {
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "kind": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                { "text": "Read the parent item to establish context.", "marks": [] }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "kind": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                { "text": "Descend into the numbered sub-step.", "marks": [] }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "kind": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                { "text": "Return to the enclosing bullet without losing your place.", "marks": [] }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "kind": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        { "text": "A sibling nested item with no deeper children, so the recursion has a base case at every level.", "marks": [] }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                { "text": "A final flat item closing the outer list.", "marks": [] }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Reading-order guarantees hold at every depth: the normalized text substrate joins items and their content blocks in document order, so a selection that begins in an outer item and ends inside a nested sub-step addresses one contiguous passage, and the markers themselves stay purely presentational.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Use this article to verify that highlighting threads through each level: a span that crosses from the outer bullet into the numbered sub-step renders marks on both levels while sharing one highlight identity.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "footnotes": []
}
